;; spec:   stdlib §4.1 (row Long/bitCount), §3 N12; lib/Long.fib (the decision in its header)
;; expect: reject
;; error:  cannot unify i32 with i64
;; roots:  ../../lib
;; covers: Long/bitCount
;; Java's Long.bitCount widens an int to a long before it counts, so (Long/bitCount -1) of an int -1
;; is 64. The builtin popcount counts at the width of its operand and would say 32 for an i32. Rather
;; than answer at a width Java does not, Long/bitCount takes an i64 and the checker refuses an i32
;; (nothing widens in fibber: write (sext i64 x) to say what Java says). The row of the table writes
;; the signature as `t -> t | Bits t`; the module's header records why it is narrower.
(ns main (:use fib.core) (:require [Long :as Long]))

(defun main () -> i64
  (Long/bitCount -1i32))
